{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumCycleBasis()"},"abstract":[{"text":"A minimum cycle basis (de Pina 1995): ","type":"text"},{"code":"edgeCount - vertexCount + c","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cycles, for c","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"components, independent over GF(2) and spanning the cycle space, with the fewest edges in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"total of any such basis. Self-loops and parallel edges are supported: a loop is a cycle of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its own, and two copies of an edge form a cycle of length 2. Each cycle starts at its least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order and leaves it through the lesser of its two edges there; the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cycles come in nondecreasing length, then by their edge positions. Ties between equally","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"short cycles are broken by the rows’ order.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6CyclesE17minimumCycleBasisSay5Walks0E0Vy6VertexQz5Edges_5IndexQZGGyF","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Cycles"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumCycleBasis","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Cycle","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks5CycleV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s: